ething that  still um remains to be fully determined  and so that i would just like to  conclude by sort of acknowledging uh  what i think has been really a a  central tenet of immunology um for for a  long time which is that inflammation is  self-limiting and that interference  gamma helps threshold responses by  activating compensatory immune  mechanisms in multiple  cell types both local to the challenge  and distant and that the combination of  these mechanisms together maintain the  fidelity of the immune response and an  appropriate return to tissue homeostasis  what i've shown you here today is that  non-hematopoietic pdl-1  limits effector t cell function in tumor  microenvironments um the endothelial  cells are a major component of this  non-hematopoietic pdl-1  and that pdl1 is driven by on all  lymphatic endothelial cells by their  exquisite um  sensitivity  to interferon gamma produced locally  within the tumor microenvironment  and that by interrupting the ability of  the lymphatic endothelium to sense the  cytotoxic immune response we can  actually drive more durable and  persistent tumor control in urine  melanomas  and with that i will just uh thank my  group this work was done by ryan lane  who's a talented uh graduate student in  the lab um and we're of course uh  they're interested in continuing to  understand the role of interfering gamma  and pdl-1 on endothelial cells  in the context of tumors and  non-malignant inflammation  thank you

