ed the b16 f10 murine melanoma which  is a poor responder to single agent  immunotherapy and we did not see a  significant change into in tumor growth  in these chimeras  but when we actually started to explore  the correlates of response within these  mice what we began to appreciate is that  both the non-hematopoietic knockout as  well as the hematopoietic knockout  enabled a  reinvigoration of a cd8 t cell response  within the tumor  associated with enhanced expression of  activation markers including pdf one  um suggesting that both pdo one from  hematopoietic and non-metaphoric cells  has a role to play  in controlling the anti-tumor t cell  response  what was interesting however is if we  looked outside the tumor  at circulating lymphocytes either in the  in the draining lymph node in the spleen  or in the blood  here we saw that only the hematopoietic  knockout  had really mobilized increased systemic  response to the tumor  whereas the non-metabolic response  looked similar  on circulating t-cell populations and  this suggested the anatomical  compartmentalization  of pdl-1  and and more recent work from ira  mellman's group and others consistent  with this that suggests that  hematopoietic pedia one plays a dominant  role in limiting the expansion of a cd  antigen-specific cd positive t cell  response and that we would then suggest  that non-hematopoietic pdl-1 including  that expressed by the endothelial cells  controls local t cell function  at the inflamed site  to eliminate the role of this systemic  priming on the effect that we were  seeing we activated antigen-specific t  cells in this case the ot-1 transgenic t  cell and transferred them into  tumor-bearing mice that expressed the  matched tumor antigen  um  what we saw is that when we do this  these t cells of course accumulate  within the tumor micro environment  directly  and  exhibit improved tumor control over wild  type mice in both the non-hematopoietic  and hematopoietic compartment  providi